{
  "summary": "Updates the functional test framework to wait for all enabled background indices (such as txindex and blockfilterindex) to sync by default during node startup and when calling `sync_all()`. It cleans up redundant manual index-synchronization calls across multiple test files and removes the standalone `sync_txindex` helper.",
  "problem": "Functional tests relying on background indices can race against wallet or RPC operations if an index has not caught up to the chain tip, causing intermittent test flakes such as missing block filters during fast wallet rescans (#36564). Previously, tests had to remember to call manual `wait_until` index checks or helpers.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description links to failure report in issue #36564 and provides a reproduction snippet using a sleep in `TraceThread` that triggers `(WARNING: block filter not found!)`.",
    "Commit fa74dc72d9 notes: 'The tests already wait for the mempool and blocks after start and after mining, so they should wait for indexes as well to avoid intermittent test failures.'"
  ],
